              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سلطان (sulṭān) is built on the native Arabic root s-l-ṭ (Lane), \"to have power over\". Lane gives sulṭān first as power and proof, then the one who holds power; Aramaic shulṭānā, power, is usually cited beside it."
