          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بلاط (balāṭ) is given by Lane under b-l-ṭ as stones laid for paving. It was borrowed from Aramaic pallāṭīn (EtymDB); the sense of a royal court is usually traced further to Latin palatium, a palace."
